    "q-3564": {
      "dom_id": "step-q3564",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n{(2{t}^{2}-3s)}^{4}=A{t}^{8}+B{t}^{6}s+C{t}^{4}{s}^{2}-216{t}^{2}{s}^{3}+81{s}^{4}\n$$\n\nwhere $A,B$ and $C$ are constants, determine the value of $A+B+C.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=4,$ $a=2{t}^{2},$ and $b=-3s.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{4}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{3}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{3},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThe $4$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,4,6,4,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{t}^{2}-3s)^{4} & =1{a}^{4}+4{a}^{3}b+6{a}^{2}{b}^{2}+4a{b}^{3}+1{b}^{4} \\\\  & =1{(2{t}^{2})}^{4}(-3s)^{0}+4{(2{t}^{2})}^{3}(-3s)^{1}+6{(2{t}^{2})}^{2}(-3s)^{2} \\\\  & \\,+4{(2{t}^{2})}^{1}(-3s)^{3}+1{(2{t}^{2})}^{0}(-3s)^{4} \\\\  & =1(16{t}^{8})(1)+4(8{t}^{6})(-3s)+6(4{t}^{4})(9{s}^{2}) \\\\  & \\,+4(2{t}^{2})(-27{s}^{3})+1(1)(81{s}^{4}) \\\\  & =16{t}^{8}-96{t}^{6}s+216{t}^{4}{s}^{2}-216{t}^{2}{s}^{3}+81{s}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=16,B=-96,$ and $C=216.$ Finally,\n\n$$\nA+B+C=16-96+216=136.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
