    "q-12884": {
      "dom_id": "step-q12884",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find, in descending powers of $y$ and ascending powers of $x,$ the first three terms of the binomial expansion of ${(y-x)}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's compare our expression with the binomial\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}.\n$$\n\nHere we have that $n=3,$ $a=y,$ and $b=-x.$ So, the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}{b}^{0},\\,{a}^{2}{b}^{1},\\,{a}^{1}{b}^{2},\\,{a}^{0}{b}^{3}.\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,3,3,1).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(y-x)}^{3} & =1{a}^{3}+3{a}^{2}b+3a{b}^{2}+1{b}^{3} \\\\  & =1(y)^{3}(-x)^{0}+3(y)^{2}(-x)^{1}+3(y)^{1}(-x)^{2}+1(y)^{0}(-x)^{3} \\\\  & =1({y}^{3})(1)+3({y}^{2})(-x)+3(y)({x}^{2})+1(1)(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & ={y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}x+3y{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in descending powers of $y$ and ascending powers of $x,$ the first three terms are\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}x+3y{x}^{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-12884-a",
